// VK_MOE_PF_VARIANT selects the prefill kernel implementation (issue
// #76): 0 = baseline, 1 = register-staged pipeline + padded sA,
// 2 = variant 1 with a 32-wide gateup N tile, 3 = producer/consumer
// wavefront-specialised gateup, 4 = variant 2 with a 16-wide gateup N
// tile, 5 = variant 4 plus a 32-wide down N tile.
//
// The default is 5.  The prefill gateup kernel is latency-bound at the
// shapes that matter (at M=2048, ispp=512 the 64-wide tile launches
// only 64 x 8 = 512 blocks, i.e. ~1.7 resident wavefronts per SIMD),
// and the N tile is the only knob that adds parallelism without adding
// work: total dequant and MFMA work is independent of the N tile,
// while a 16-wide gateup tile cuts the accumulator footprint and
// quadruples the grid.  Measured on MI300A (see
// docs/performance/moe-fused/gfx942.md): 2.67x at M=128, 1.79x at
// M=512, 1.83x at M=1024, 1.66x at M=2048 over variant 0.  The 32-wide
// gateup tile is ~1.4% faster at M=2048 and much slower below it, so
// 16-wide is the better single default; both are within run-to-run
// variance of each other at the largest M.
static const int pf_variant = [] {
  const char* s = std::getenv("VK_MOE_PF_VARIANT");
  return s ? std::atoi(s) : 5;
}();

