// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
// Register-staged variants of the prefill tile movers (issue #76).
//
// The baseline prefill loop above touches global in three separate phases
// per kb (load sA, dequant gate, MFMA gate, dequant up, MFMA up) with four
// barriers, and the two dequant phases each expose the full cold-DRAM
// latency of the packed weight stream.  With the prefill grid at ~1.7
// blocks/CU there are not enough resident warps to hide it: profiling
// shows ~70% of wave-cycles in SQ_WAIT_ANY.
//
// These helpers stage iter kb+1's packed fp4 bytes + ue8m0 scales + the A
// tile in REGISTERS while iter kb's dequant/MFMA execute (same technique as
// the decode PrefBTile, one iteration deeper for the 64x64 tile).  The
// loop then has a single latency-free store/dequant phase and one barrier
// pair per kb instead of two serialised global round trips.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
// Issue #76 v2: N-tile-parameterised register-staged B movers.
//
// The prefill grid is (EM / kBM_pf) x (ispp / kBN) blocks.  With kBN=64
// that is 64 x 8 = 512 blocks at M=2048, i.e. only ~1.7 wavefronts per
// SIMD on MI300 -- fewer than the latency of a packed-weight DRAM read,
// so the schedule is bound by exposed memory/ALU latency rather than by
// throughput.  The total dequant work is
//     (EM / kBM) * ispp * hidden          (independent of kBN)
// so halving the N tile doubles the grid (1024 blocks) for free and, at
// kNF = kBN/16 = 2, quarters the per-thread accumulator footprint.
//
//   n = tid & (kBN-1),  kp = (tid / kBN) + it * (kThreads_pf / kBN)
// so kBN=64 gives 8 packed + 8 scale bytes/thread and kBN=32 gives 4+4.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------
template <int kBN>
struct PrefB_pfT {
  static constexpr int kBytesPerThread = (kBK_pf / 2) * kBN / kThreads_pf;
  uint8_t pb[kBytesPerThread];
  uint8_t sc[kBytesPerThread];
};

